  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb, reflexive — follows standard endings in every tense, no exceptions.",
    "Almost always used with \"en\": *basarse en algo* (\"to be based on something\").",
    "Past participle is regular: **basado**.",
    "Imperativo afirmativo reflexive pronouns attach to the end with a written accent to preserve stress (básate, básese, basémonos, básense); imperativo negativo places them separately in front (no te bases...).",
    "*La película se basa en una historia real.* (\"The movie is based on a true story.\")",
    "*Nos basamos en los datos del informe.* (\"We're basing this on the report's data.\")",
    "Related: *la base* (base/basis, noun), *basar* (non-reflexive, \"to base something on\"), *fundamentar* (synonym, \"to substantiate/ground\")."
  ],
